#lego-legacy-route 1
# Hot Wheels Stunt Track Driver, from a clean profile through Championship
# Tracks 1-6, unlocking and finishing the hidden 7th track (WIRE), and out on
# Escape (#285).
#
# Space at flip 285 skips the intro to the main menu; clicks at 385, 463, 539,
# 569, 631 and 696 enter Championship mode and launch Track 1 (Living Room).
# The route drives all six Championship tracks to the finish on the unmodified
# retail binary, writing saves\times.dat after each race (flips 3245, 5704,
# 8330, 10767, 14301 and 16598) and saves\onoff.dat at flips 8330 and 16598,
# leaving all six tracks unlocked (01 00 00 00 x 6 + 00 00 00 00, 28 bytes).
#
# From Championship completion it returns to the main menu (17711), opens Track
# Select (17811), moves the pointer onto the invisible Mattel "TT" logo hotspot
# and right-clicks at flip 17889 (down right / up right at 17894) to arm Secret
# Track 7 (WIRE.JAM, neon-green wireframe grid). Flip 17919 holds Track Select
# with the pointer on the Mattel logo; clicks at 17925 and 17999 confirm the
# track and car. WIRE starts on the grid (flip 18125), performs an inverted
# barrel roll over the wireframe valley (flip 18460), runs the wireframe tunnel
# at speed (flip 19750), and crosses the finish line with 04 stunts and 0
# crashes, writing saves\times.dat at flip 20756 and presenting the 1:16 Bronze
# Medal results screen (flip 20976). Escape at flip 20977 quits cleanly three
# flips later (exited 1 at flip 20980).
